text:
Each `_has` clause is evaluated independently, so different Observations can satisfy separate clauses. Thus q1 includes pt-2, whose HbA1c supplies the code match and glucose supplies the value match. In q3, pt-5’s final Observation o-7 satisfies the status clause despite o-6 being entered-in-error.

The composite ties code and quantity to the same Observation. Chaining in q4 requires a resolvable female Patient. Includes add existing referenced resources; reverse includes are not recursive without `:iterate`, so q7 does not add provenance for its included Observations.

```json
{
  "q1": [
    "Patient/pt-1",
    "Patient/pt-2",
    "Patient/pt-3",
    "Patient/pt-5"
  ],
  "q2": [
    "Patient/pt-1",
    "Patient/pt-3",
    "Patient/pt-5"
  ],
  "q3": [
    "Patient/pt-1",
    "Patient/pt-3",
    "Patient/pt-5"
  ],
  "q4": [
    "Observation/o-1",
    "Observation/o-5"
  ],
  "q5": {
    "match": [
      "Observation/o-1",
      "Observation/o-5",
      "Observation/o-6",
      "Observation/o-8"
    ],
    "include": [
      "Patient/pt-1",
      "Patient/pt-3",
      "Patient/pt-5"
    ]
  },
  "q6": {
    "match": [
      "Observation/o-3",
      "Observation/o-4"
    ],
    "include": [
      "Provenance/prov-2"
    ]
  },
  "q7": {
    "match": [
      "Patient/pt-1",
      "Patient/pt-3"
    ],
    "include": [
      "Observation/o-1",
      "Observation/o-2",
      "Observation/o-5",
      "Provenance/prov-3"
    ]
  }
}
```

